{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"N29\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N30\",\"lines\":\"r--n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N30.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"عِندَهَا\",\"after\":\"The rare sense of قَوْمًا as uprightness meets عِندَهَا as turning away from what is right. The people’s setting can carry a moral tension between standing straight and resisting the truth.\",\"reason\":\"The branch gives قَوْمًا the sense of استقامة واعتدال, while عِندَهَا is glossed as عدول عن الاستقامة وممانعة للحق. Straightness and defiance of the straight path are opposites.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N30.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"حُسْنًا\",\"after\":\"Goodness reads as a broad ethical form of uprightness among the people.\",\"reason\":\"The rare قَوْمًا sense is استقامة, or staying on a straight and balanced way; حُسْنًا names الإحسان, doing good. They share an ethical direction, though they do not name one specific act.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N31\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N32\",\"lines\":\"----\"}\n{\"id\":\"N33\",\"lines\":\"--r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N33.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"حُسْنًا\",\"after\":\"The rare قَوْمًا sense evokes a person’s handsome, well-formed stature, while حُسْنًا names goodness and excellence. The choice of goodness among the people can thus appear as a fine form given to the group.\",\"reason\":\"The branch describes قوام الجسم and حسن القامة; the target حُسْنًا is الإحسان فعل حسن. Bodily good form and moral goodness make one image without becoming the same sense.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N34\",\"lines\":\"rr-n-r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N34.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"عَيْنٍ\",\"after\":\"The sun is found setting in an عَيْنٍ that can mean a spring or water source. The rare قامة as a pulley for drawing water makes that source part of a working well scene.\",\"reason\":\"The branch includes القامة البكرة التي يستقى بها الماء, a pulley used to draw water; عَيْنٍ is a flowing spring. The mechanism and the source complement each other in the image of a well.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N34.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"حَمِئَةٍ\",\"after\":\"The traveler reaches a حَمِئَةٍ spring of black mud, with the rare قامة as a pulley at the well. The practical water-drawing image sets the dark, muddy horizon beside a working mechanism.\",\"reason\":\"The rare branch names a pulley used to draw water and even places its supporting form at a well’s edge; حَمِئَةٍ describes dark, muddy water. Together they picture a pulley above a muddy source.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N34.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْقَرْنَيْنِ\",\"after\":\"The rare قوام as a support piece and ٱلْقَرْنَيْنِ as joining suggest parts held in a linked structure.\",\"reason\":\"The focus sense is a supporting or handled part, آلة قائمة وجزء قائم; the target’s plain sense is جمع شيء إلى شيء وربطه به. A component can belong to an assembly, though the link stays pictorial.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N34.6\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"تَتَّخِذَ\",\"after\":\"The option is to adopt goodness, and تَتَّخِذَ also carries the sense of taking or acquiring. A handle is the part by which something is taken hold of, so goodness can appear as something actively grasped.\",\"reason\":\"The rare قَوْمًا branch includes قائم السيف مقبضه, a handle, while تَتَّخِذَ means الاتخاذ والاكتساب. The handle is a tool for taking hold, linking the concrete implement to the verb’s plain sense.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N35\",\"lines\":\"---r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N35.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"تُعَذِّبَ\",\"after\":\"The punishment option falls under the shadow of a day when people stand before God for judgment. The rare sense of قَوْمًا makes this choice echo the larger reckoning and its punishment.\",\"reason\":\"The branch is القيامة, the day when creation rises before God; تُعَذِّبَ names inflicting punishment. Punishment is an outcome associated with judgment, so the two senses meet as an event and one of its consequences.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N36\",\"lines\":\"-nr-n-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N36.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"وَوَجَدَ\",\"after\":\"The finding of a people can open a scene of face-to-face contest, though this clause does not say that they resist.\",\"reason\":\"The rare قَوْمًا sense is مقاومة ومنازلة, mutual resistance; وَوَجَدَ means finding or encountering the people. Encounter provides a setting for resistance, but that connection is general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N36.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"عِندَهَا\",\"after\":\"The rare sense of قَوْمًا carries mutual resistance, while عِندَهَا is glossed as opposition to what is right. The encounter is colored by resistance before the choice of punishment or goodness is announced.\",\"reason\":\"The focus branch is قاومته, to contend with someone; the target sense is عدول عن الاستقامة وممانعة للحق. Both name resistance, making the overlap direct.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N36.5\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْقَرْنَيْنِ\",\"after\":\"Resistance sets two sides against each other, while the joining sense of ٱلْقَرْنَيْنِ can picture those sides bound into one contest.\",\"reason\":\"The rare focus sense is مقاومة ومنازلة, and the target’s plain sense is جمع شيء إلى شيء وربطه به. The image of a contest joins opponents, but the relation is broad.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N37\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N38\",\"lines\":\"nrr--\"}\n{\"id\":\"N38.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"بَلَغَ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense of قَوْمًا includes water standing still and an exhausted animal stopping; بَلَغَ names reaching an endpoint. Arrival can suggest a halt at the limit of the journey.\",\"reason\":\"The Arabic examples قام الماء جمد and قامت الدابة وقفت describe stillness or stopping; بَلَغَ is الوصول إلى الغاية. Reaching and stopping can meet at a journey’s endpoint, though the link is general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N38.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"عَيْنٍ\",\"after\":\"عَيْنٍ can be a flowing spring, while the rare قَوْمًا sense describes water that has frozen or stopped. The spring’s source and the still water stand against one another in the dark setting scene.\",\"reason\":\"The branch includes قام الماء جمد, water becoming still; عَيْنٍ is a spring or منبع الماء الجاري. The stillness of one sense opposes the flow of the other.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N38.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"حَمِئَةٍ\",\"after\":\"The rare قَوْمًا sense is water standing still, and حَمِئَةٍ names black, muddy water. Together they make a picture of a stagnant dark pool at the sun’s setting.\",\"reason\":\"The branch says قام الماء جمد, while حَمِئَةٍ is الحمأة السوداء في الماء. Still water and dark mud meet in the image of a motionless, muddy source.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N39\",\"lines\":\"rrrn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N39.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"مَغْرِبَ\",\"after\":\"The rare قَوْمًا sense places the sun at noon, while مَغْرِبَ names its setting place or time. The pair stretches from the sun’s height at midday to its disappearance in the west.\",\"reason\":\"The focus branch is انتصاف النهار, the middle of the day; the target is غروب الشمس والمغرب. Noon and sunset mark opposite points in the sun’s daily course.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N39.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلشَّمْسِ\",\"after\":\"The rare قَوْمًا sense is the moment when the sun stands overhead at noon. Hearing it beside ٱلشَّمْسِ brings the sun’s daily arc into view, from its high point toward its setting.\",\"reason\":\"The branch describes قامت الشمس وكاد الظل يعقل, the sun at midday; ٱلشَّمْسِ is the sun itself. Noon is a stage in the sun’s course.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N39.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"تَغْرُبُ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense sets the sun at midday, while تَغْرُبُ names its setting. The two moments mark opposing directions in the ayah’s movement across the sun’s course.\",\"reason\":\"The focus branch is انتصاف النهار, and the target is غروب الشمس. A sun at its noon height is the counterpart of a sun going down.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N39.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"عَيْنٍ\",\"after\":\"The midday sun and عَيْنٍ as an eye can briefly form the image of عين الشمس, the sun’s eye.\",\"reason\":\"The rare قَوْمًا sense is قائم الظهيرة, the sun at midday; عَيْنٍ can mean an eye. The image is possible, though the verse’s scene is sunset at a spring.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N40\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N41\",\"lines\":\"-r-r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N41.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"عَيْنٍ\",\"after\":\"The rare قَوْمًا sense names pain borne by a body part, including the eyes. Since عَيْنٍ can mean an eye, the muddy spring can briefly carry an embodied eye-image, as though it were an afflicted eye.\",\"reason\":\"The branch gives قامت بي عيناي, “my eyes hurt”; عَيْنٍ can name العين الناظرة. The eye is a body part that can bear the pain in the focus sense.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N41.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"تُعَذِّبَ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense describes pain lodged in a bodily member, while تُعَذِّبَ is the act of inflicting punishment. The offered punishment is heard through the pain it brings to the body.\",\"reason\":\"The branch says كل ما أوجعك من جسدك فقد قام بك, whatever hurts in the body has come upon it; تُعَذِّبَ names إيلام وعقوبة. Bodily pain is part of the punishment’s effect.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N42\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N43\",\"lines\":\"rr-r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N43.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"مَغْرِبَ\",\"after\":\"The rare قَوْمًا sense is an eye that has lost its sight although its pupil remains. Beside مَغْرِبَ, the sun’s disappearance at the west supplies an image for sight going out while the eye remains.\",\"reason\":\"The focus branch is عين قائمة ذهب بصرها والحدقة صحيحة; the target is the sun’s setting place. The physical eye persists as the light disappears, linking blindness with sunset.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N43.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"عَيْنٍ\",\"after\":\"The rare قَوْمًا sense is an eye whose sight has vanished despite its intact pupil; عَيْنٍ can mean a seeing eye. The word is read as a spring in the scene, but its eye sense lets sight be present and gone at once.\",\"reason\":\"The focus branch is عين قائمة ذهب بصرها والحدقة صحيحة, while the target’s eye sense is العين الناظرة. A sightless eye and a seeing eye are opposites.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N43.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"target_ar\":\"تَتَّخِذَ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense describes the loss of sight, while تَتَّخِذَ carries taking or acquiring. The option to adopt goodness can sound like a gain set against the eye’s loss.\",\"reason\":\"In the focus branch, the eye loses بصَرها; the target’s plain sense is الاتخاذ والاكتساب. Loss of a faculty and acquisition stand in opposition, and the ayah gives that acquisition a moral object.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N44\",\"lines\":\"----\"}\n{\"id\":\"N45\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N46\",\"lines\":\"--rr---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N46.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"قُلْنَا\",\"target_ar\":\"عَيْنٍ\",\"after\":\"The sun is found setting into عَيْنٍ, a spring or water source, while قُلّة is a large water jar. Source and vessel complete one water image, as though the spring fed a jar at the horizon.\",\"reason\":\"The rare قُلّة sense is القلة الجرة الكبيرة, a large jar; عَيْنٍ can mean منبع الماء الجاري. A container and the source that fills it complement one another.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N46.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قُلْنَا\",\"target_ar\":\"حَمِئَةٍ\",\"after\":\"A large قُلّة can hold the water named by حَمِئَةٍ, the dark muddy spring. The jar brings the sun’s strange setting close as a vessel filled at a muddy source.\",\"reason\":\"The focus sense is a large water jar, while حَمِئَةٍ names black, foul-smelling mud in water. Their senses meet in the image of a vessel at the dark spring.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N47\",\"lines\":\"nr-r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N47.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قُلْنَا\",\"target_ar\":\"عِندَهَا\",\"after\":\"استقل can mean setting out, while عِندَهَا is glossed as turning away from straightness. The shared movement is departure from a line, physical in one sense and moral in the other.\",\"reason\":\"The focus branch has استقل القوم مضوا وارتحلوا, people setting out; the target sense is عدول عن الاستقامة. Departure and deviation meet as a directional image.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N47.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"قُلْنَا\",\"target_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"after\":\"The rare sense includes the phrase استقل القوم, “the people set out,” while قَوْمًا names the people. Beside Dhu al-Qarnayn’s journey to this endpoint, the group he finds can briefly appear as another traveling party before the ayah turns to their treatment.\",\"reason\":\"The focus branch describes a group departing or carrying loads; قَوْمًا is a collective of people. The group supplies the agent for the journey action, making a compact travel image.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N47.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قُلْنَا\",\"target_ar\":\"تَتَّخِذَ\",\"after\":\"تَتَّخِذَ is to adopt or acquire, while the rare sense can be to lift and carry something. The goodness offered to the people can appear as something they take up and bear.\",\"reason\":\"The focus branch includes أقل الجرة أطاق حملها, being able to carry a jar; the target means الاتخاذ والاكتساب. Carrying and adopting meet in the image of taking goodness on as a load.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N48\",\"lines\":\"----\"}\n{\"id\":\"N49\",\"lines\":\"-r--\"}\n{\"id\":\"N49.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"قُلْنَا\",\"target_ar\":\"عَيْنٍ\",\"after\":\"The rare قَوْل sense is the tongue, the organ of speech, while عَيْنٍ can mean the eye. In the ayah, the setting is found and then speech follows, so seeing and saying complete one another.\",\"reason\":\"The focus branch names اللسان آلة القول; the target can be العين الناظرة. Eye and tongue are distinct organs, and the scene’s perception is answered by the declaration قُلْنَا.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N50\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N51\",\"lines\":\"-r-n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N51.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"قُلْنَا\",\"target_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"after\":\"The rare قيل is a ruler whose word carries authority, while قَوْمًا names a people. The choice of how to treat them becomes a scene of authority exercised over a community.\",\"reason\":\"The focus branch is القيل صاحب القول النافذ, a ruler whose speech takes effect; the target is جماعة الناس. A ruler and the people subject to his decision form complementary roles.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N51.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"قُلْنَا\",\"target_ar\":\"حُسْنًا\",\"after\":\"The ruler’s authoritative word and حُسْنًا as kind conduct meet in the possibility of authority expressed through good treatment.\",\"reason\":\"The rare قيل is one whose word is effective; حُسْنًا names الإحسان فعل حسن. The relation is a ruler’s power alongside the good conduct he may choose.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N52\",\"lines\":\"-rn-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N52.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"قُلْنَا\",\"target_ar\":\"عِندَهَا\",\"after\":\"The rare sense of قُلْنَا includes falsely attributing words to someone, while عِندَهَا is glossed as resisting what is right. Both can be heard as refusals of truth, setting the moral choice against falsehood.\",\"reason\":\"The focus branch is قولتني ما لم أقل, falsely claiming I said what I did not; the target sense is ممانعة للحق. False attribution and resistance to truth share an anti-truth direction.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N52.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قُلْنَا\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْقَرْنَيْنِ\",\"after\":\"A false attribution attaches a claim to a speaker, while ٱلْقَرْنَيْنِ carries a joining sense; together they suggest a claim fastened to someone.\",\"reason\":\"The rare branch is قول ما لم يكن or falsely ascribing a statement; the target’s plain sense is جمع شيء إلى شيء وربطه به. The image of attaching words to a person is real, though remote from the title’s immediate scene.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N53\",\"lines\":\"n-r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N53.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"قُلْنَا\",\"target_ar\":\"وَجَدَهَا\",\"after\":\"The traveler perceives the sun setting, while the rare قَوْل sense is drawing words into oneself. Perception can precede taking in or formulating what has been perceived.\",\"reason\":\"The focus branch is اجترار القول إلى النفس, taking a saying inward; وَجَدَهَا means finding or perceiving. The senses can form a perception-to-internalization sequence, but it is general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N53.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"قُلْنَا\",\"target_ar\":\"تَتَّخِذَ\",\"after\":\"The rare قَوْل sense is drawing a saying into oneself, and تَتَّخِذَ is taking or adopting something for oneself. The option to adopt goodness can therefore sound like taking it inward as one’s own.\",\"reason\":\"The focus branch is اجتر إلى نفسه قولا, drawing words into oneself; the target means الاتخاذ والاكتساب. Both express taking something inward or for oneself, with speech in one image and goodness in the other.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N54\",\"lines\":\"nnr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N54.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"قُلْنَا\",\"target_ar\":\"قَوْمًا\",\"after\":\"The rare قَوْل sense is speech circulating among people, while قَوْمًا names a collective of people. The group supplies the public among whom such speech moves.\",\"reason\":\"The focus branch is القول الفاشي بين الناس; the target is جماعة الناس. Public talk needs a community in which to circulate, though the relation is broad.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N54.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قُلْنَا\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْقَرْنَيْنِ\",\"after\":\"A saying that circulates passes from one person to another, while ٱلْقَرْنَيْنِ carries a sense of joining. The pair can picture speech connecting its listeners.\",\"reason\":\"The rare branch is القول الفاشي بين الناس; the target means جمع شيء إلى شيء وربطه به. Circulation joins speakers and listeners, making a public utterance into a social link.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N54.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قُلْنَا\",\"target_ar\":\"حُسْنًا\",\"after\":\"The rare sense includes a حسن saying that spreads among people, while حُسْنًا is goodness or kind conduct. The good treatment offered here can become good speech that circulates among the people.\",\"reason\":\"The focus branch includes انتشرت له قالة حسنة, a favorable saying spreading about someone; the target is الإحسان فعل حسن. The ayah’s good conduct and its good public account make a fitting image.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N55\",\"lines\":\"-----\"}"}}
